 "summary": "One native run of NAT-022 canary-plain (RECOVERY image sha256 a7913234df2451e00a0cc9e8c339395e072a6897dad1aec411057021437921fe) under decision 0009. Written to /dev/block/sda18 with full readback match, one adb reboot recovery at 2026-11-10T12:11:16Z. Owner-reported observation (their words: 'вроде полос не было'; they entered Download Mode because the phone kept restarting): no stripes were seen. Host passive USB events (enumeration only, not a console): ADB device gone 12:11:20; SEC_UPLOAD (685d) enumerated 12:12:51 (~95 s after the request) with no Odin command sent; it vanished at 12:13:37 and 'SAMSUNG USB' Download Mode appeared 12:13:42 (owner action). The canary arms no watchdog, so a reset near 95 s was not caused by watchdog code in this image. Stock RECOVERY restored by one NAT-013 session (bus 5 address 34); full RECOVERY hash equals stock 96620b8b..., assess pass, sys.boot_completed=1, bootanim stopped, user 0 present, user state RUNNING_LOCKED right after boot; no personal content read. NOT established: whether the canary's first instruction ran, MMU/cache state, or why no markers were seen. Untested explanations: (a) image not executed, (b) M=1 entry where the best-effort draw failed or hit another mapping, (c) panel not scanning 0xFA200000 or command-mode needing a DECON trigger, (d) contrast invisible. No video was provided to the host, so decoding was not attempted.",
